<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sicca Veneria</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sicca, El Kef</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sicca Veneria was an ancient town in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a>, on the site of modern El Kef, named after its sanctuary of a goddess identified with Venus. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> it was where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> gathered before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary-war">Mercenary War</a> of 241 BCE, and it later belonged to the Numidian kingdom. It became a Roman colony under Augustus and an important town of the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sicca-veneria.jpg" alt="Sicca Veneria" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Moumou82 at French Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:El_Kef.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
